      "text": "To determine the possible degrees of the remainder when a polynomial is divided by \\(2x^2 - 7x + 18\\), we need to understand the polynomial division algorithm. The division of a polynomial \\(P(x)\\) by a non-zero polynomial \\(D(x)\\) can be expressed as:\n\\[P(x) = Q(x) \\cdot D(x) + R(x),\\]\nwhere \\(Q(x)\\) is the quotient and \\(R(x)\\) is the remainder. The degree of the remainder \\(R(x)\\) must be less than the degree of the divisor \\(D(x)\\).\n\nThe divisor here is \\(2x^2 - 7x + 18\\). Since it is a polynomial of degree 2, the remainder \\(R(x)\\) must be a polynomial of degree 1 or less. Therefore, the possible degrees of the remainder are 0 and 1. In other words, the possible degrees of the remainder are 0, 1, and 2, but since the degree of the remainder must be less than the degree of the divisor, the possible degrees are 0 and 1.\n\nThus, the possible degrees of the remainder are:\n\\[\n\\boxed{0, 1}\n\\]",
